<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-2383] Non-string system properties should be ignored in node attributes and update checker</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-2383</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;user@ discussion: &lt;a href=&quot;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Ignite-quot-bugs-quot-td2534.html&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;http://apache-ignite-users.70518.x6.nabble.com/Ignite-quot-bugs-quot-td2534.html&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Some frameworks can put non-string and/or non-serializable values into system properties. We should ignore them in &lt;tt&gt;GridUpdateNotifier.getSystemProperties()&lt;/tt&gt; method and when adding properties to node attributes.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
